  "text_pages": [
    "Exchange/Visiting Pre-Arrival Guide - f. Document Submission Form\nSearch this site\nEmbedded Files\nSkip to main content\nSkip to navigation\nDocument Submission\nForm\nSupporting Documents Google Form\nRequired DOcuments\nPlease include your name on each file:\nHONG_Gildong_Application.pdf\nSMITH_John_Transcripts.pdf\nSMITH_Jane_IDphoto.jpg\nIf you need to update (i.e., replace/modify) a document you already submitted, please email us the new one so we can update it for you.\nQuick Notes\nWe will edit certain parts of your application - these wi\nll appear \"blank\" to you -\nplease do NOT change these after we do:\nPassport expiration date\n- students often enter their birthdates for some reason\n;\nwe will correct this.\nYour name\n- we will make it conform to the form on your passport that is required by Immigration. This is likely not ho\nw many of you write your names - but there is a format required by law since you are not a Korean citizen.\nIndividual File Submission (.pdf, .doc, or .jpg)\nPDF version of Online Exchange Application form\nhttp://wis.hufs.ac.kr:8989/src08/jsp/fexchange/index.html\nB\nrief essay of personal history and plan of study (one page A4)\nCopy of academic transcripts\nChinese Citizens\nChinese citizens must also submit transcripts that are verified by the Chinese Education Ministry - (www.chsi.com.cn / www.cdgdc.edu.cn).\nCertificate of current enrollment at home university (Apostilled/Notarized Versions required for non-OECD nationalities)\nEvidence of proficiency in English/Korean language or reference letter if applicable\nCopy of the information page of passport\nID Photo (a standard ID photo - internal use only)\nDorm application form (if desiring a dorm space)\nHealth examination form (Dorm applicants only - you can do this once dorm assignments are announced)\n*\n*\nAll dormitory applicants must\nsubmit\ncopy of completed health form signed by the doctor and they must also present the original copy as they check-in at the HUFS dormitory. You can also do this check at a clinic near campus when you arrive for about 20,000-30,000 KRW.\nFinancial Statement (please wait for us to request this item- it is time sensitive - we will request it about 2 weeks before we plan to issue Admissions Packets (Apostilled/Notarized Versions required for non-OECD nationalities):\n4 months Exchange -\n5\n,\n0\n00 USD\n6 months Exchange -\n8\n,\n0\n00 USD\n10 months Exchange -\n13\n,000 USD\n12 months Exchange -\n16\n,000 US\nD\nLanguage Proficiency Information\nEnglish\nFor taking classes taught in English\nOne of the following:\nIELTS - overall band score of at least 6.0\nTOEFL/TOEFL ITP - 550 or higher\ncomputer-based 213 or higher\ninternet-based 80 or higher\nTOEIC - 750 or higher\nLetter from a university professor familiar both with the expected standards of an English-medium university program and with the student's ability to perform in an English-medium academic atmosphere.\nKorean\nFor taking classes taught in Korean\nOne of the following:\nTOPIK 3+\nKLAT 150+ (B2)\n15 hours (4-5 classes) of university-level Korean language courses (e.g., Korean 101, 102, 201, 202, 301)\nHUFS Intensive Korean Program Level 4 Certificate\nNo requirements for taking Intensive Korean Language only\nApplication Demo (English)\nApplication Demo (Korean)\nReport abuse\nPage details\nPage updated\nReport abuse"
  ],
